  "readme": "# B1F1 follow-up stopped before Worker readiness\n\nThe original actual runtime26019 exited1(3abcab) at the existing20-second Worker readiness boundary:5198 refused connections. The server child remained alive until owned cleanup; server.log is zero bytes, so the responsible startup stage/cause is unknown. Firefox, driver and recorder never spawned; completed cases/media are zero. The RGB/CRF0/LP2 source request is not an actual lossless or pixel result. No runtime replay followed.\n\nAn earlier owner CLI path typo failed before reading the authorized release or creating attempt-1. Its original stderr and stdout remain separate. Root inspected the exact missing-path error, correct release hash and absence of an attempt/owned roles before explicitly authorizing the corrected first actual attempt. Source, release and attempt number were unchanged.\n\nRoot independently reverified all34,322 tracked data files,312 canonical files,234 dist files,22 protected files,9 tool guards and63 runtime bindings; supervisor/Xvfb/server PID and PGIDs, readable escaped markers,5198 and private root/profile/authority were closed/absent. Foreign environment permission limits are explicit. Early handles do not persist the assigned displayfd value; existing X0/X1 sockets are observations, not a guessed test-display identity. No owned PID remains in any readable X lock.\n\nThere were zero memory observations before this early failure. The stored zero peak is not an observed live zero RSS, and minimum available memory is unknown. The failed run, original empty server log, Xvfb warnings and precise lifecycle limits stay intact. The display-registration and startup-stage logging proposal has no execution authority.\n\nThe source-v1 static success-capture-count defect and the accepted v2 source peer remain separate. All immutable producer bytes use lossless gzip storage without whitespace normalization. Two large full preparation responses stay locally intact and hash-bound; norma